# Authentication UX Rule

Account is an authenticated area.

When an unauthenticated user taps the Account tab:

- DO NOT render the authenticated Account screen.
- Redirect the user to the existing Login screen/route.

After successful authentication:

- Return the user to Account, or
- Return them to their original intended destination if they came from another protected action.

The Account screen itself must also verify authentication so that protected content cannot be accessed by directly navigating to its route.

Do not duplicate authentication logic. Reuse the existing auth/session state and navigation utilities in:

- `src/features/auth/utils/authNavigation.ts`
- `src/features/auth/hooks/useRequireAuth.ts`

Apply the same authentication-gating principle to:

- Orders
- Profile
- Addresses
- Checkout
- Place Order
- Other authenticated-only actions

Do not change the authentication API or business logic.

For guest users, never display fake/empty authenticated account information just to populate the Account screen.

The UX should clearly communicate why authentication is required.

## Auth-gated action policy

| Action         | Guest   | Logged in |
| -------------- | ------- | --------- |
| Home           | Yes     | Yes       |
| Categories     | Yes     | Yes       |
| Search         | Yes     | Yes       |
| Product Detail | Yes     | Yes       |
| Cart           | Yes     | Yes       |
| Account        | Login   | Yes       |
| Orders         | Login   | Yes       |
| Profile        | Login   | Yes       |
| Addresses      | Login   | Yes       |
| Checkout       | Login   | Yes       |
| Place Order    | Login   | Yes       |

## Return-to pattern

When redirecting guests to Login, pass an `AuthReturnTo` destination via `openAuthLogin(navigation, returnTo)`.

After OTP verification, `completeAuthNavigation` dismisses the auth modal and navigates to the preserved destination.

Example: guest cart checkout flow:

```
Checkout -> not logged in -> Login -> successful login -> Payment
```

Do not dump users on Account after login when they intended Checkout or another protected action.
